{"photo-bighorn-ram-full-curl":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bighorn-ram-full-curl.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: YellowstoneNPS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bighorn_sheep_ram_in_winter_(53481643872).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bighorn ram. Heavy curled horns, brown body, white rump. Ram classes and curl rules: see the Rule Book."},"photo-dalls-sheep-ram":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/dalls-sheep-ram.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Jacob W. Frank, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Closeup_of_a_Dall_sheep_ram_(08f0a8ea-88cd-44d1-973c-49248da0d61f).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Dall sheep ram. All white body, pale flaring horns. In BC only in the far northwest."},"photo-stones-sheep-ram":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/stones-sheep-ram.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Jack Bindernagel, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ovis_dalli_stonei_321175932.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Stone's sheep ram. Dark body, white rump, belly and leg backs. Northern BC."},"photo-mountain-goat-billy":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/mountain-goat-billy.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Forest Service Alaska Region, USDA, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountain_Goat-Tongass-BLL-018_(52502328982).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mountain goat. White coat, short black dagger horns, beard. Not a sheep: sheep have curled brown or amber horns."},"photo-mule-deer-buck":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/mule-deer-buck.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: GlacierNPS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_Deer_Buck_(43010371115).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mule deer buck: big mule ears, antlers that fork and fork again, rope tail with a black tip."},"photo-g-md-buck-front":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-buck-front.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Matt Reinbold from USA, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:I_Think_He%27s_Noticed_Me_(3875851465).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mule deer buck. Big mule ears, white throat patch, antlers that branch in forks (each beam splits, then splits again)."},"photo-g-wt-doe":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-doe.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service - Midwest Region, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White-tailed_deer_(54365597311).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"White tailed doe. No antlers, smaller ears than a mule deer, long wide brown tail with white edges."},"photo-g-wt-buck-side":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-buck-side.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Famartin, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2025-11-09_07_48_17_White-tailed_Deer_buck_in_autumn_along_Aquetong_Lane_in_the_Mountainview_section_of_Ewing_Township,_Mercer_County,_New_Jersey.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"White tailed buck. Smaller ears, wide brown tail with white edges, tines that grow up off one main beam."},"photo-g-moose-bull-side":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-moose-bull-side.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Jacob W. Frank, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alces_alces_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bull moose. Black brown, horse sized, shoulder hump, long face, wide palmated (flat, hand shaped) antlers."},"photo-g-moose-cow":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-moose-cow.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: naturenps, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cow_moose_(33233257795).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Cow moose. No antlers, long legs, big nose, often with a calf. Look for the pale patch under the tail."},"photo-g-elk-bull-side":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-elk-bull-side.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Wilson Hui from Calgary, Canada, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bull_Elk_Stag_(32272946993).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bull elk. Tan body, dark brown neck and mane, straw coloured rump, long antlers swept back over the body."},"photo-g-elk-cow":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-elk-cow.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: GlacierNPS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cow_Elk_Glacier_National_Park.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Cow elk. No antlers, tan body, dark head and neck, pale rump. Much bigger than a deer, smaller than a moose."},"photo-g-bb-side":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bb-side.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Charles J. Sharp, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olympic_black_bear_(Ursus_americanus_altifrontalis)_male_Whistler.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Black bear. No shoulder hump, straight face profile, tall ears, short curved claws. Colour does NOT tell you the species."},"photo-g-griz-front":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-griz-front.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: NPS/Jim Peaco, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:File-Grizzly_bear_on_Swan_Lake_Flats;-Jim_Peaco;-June_2005;-Catalog_18220d;-Original_IT8M3358_(f3aced99-1dd8-b71b-0bfc-4ad5c6105cb2).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Grizzly bear. Shoulder hump, dished (concave) face, short round ears, long pale claws. Often silver tipped fur."},"photo-g-md-buck-side":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-md-buck-side.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Marshal Hedin from San Diego, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mule_deer_buck_(Odocoileus_hemionus),_Little_Shasta,_Siskiyou_County_CA_(24178985295).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mule deer buck. Grey brown, white rump patch, thin white tail with a black tip, antlers that fork."},"photo-g-bt-doe":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bt-doe.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Walter Siegmund (talk), CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Odocoileus_hemionus_5432.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Black tailed deer. Coast deer. Tail wider than a mule deer's and dark or black all the way down the top."},"photo-g-bt-buck":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bt-buck.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Philip Cohen, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Columbian_Black-tailed_Deer_buck.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Black tailed buck. Forked antlers like a mule deer, but a smaller, darker deer with a wide tail dark all down the top."},"photo-g-quail-male-vernon":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-quail-male-vernon.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Alan D. Wilson, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:California_Quail_(Male).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"California quail male. Black teardrop plume, black face with a white border, grey chest, scaly belly."},"photo-g-quail-female":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-quail-female.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Alan Vernon, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Callipepla_californica_-California,_USA_-female_and_chick-_8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"California quail female. Plain grey brown face, short plume, scaly belly. Often with a covey of young."},"photo-g-chukar":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-chukar.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Artemy Voikhansky, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chukar_partridge.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Chukar. Grey partridge sized bird with red legs and bill, black eye stripe and necklace, barred sides. Lives on steep rocky slopes."},"photo-g-spruce-male":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-spruce-male.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Mdf, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Falcipennis-canadensis-002.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Spruce grouse male. Dark grey and black, black throat edged in white, red comb. Very tame. Conifer forest."},"photo-g-ptarmigan-summer":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-ptarmigan-summer.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS - Pacific Region, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Rainier_White-Tailed_Ptarmigan_(53058740798).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"White tailed ptarmigan. Small alpine grouse. Mottled brown in summer, all white in winter, white tail all year."},"photo-g-pheasant-rooster":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-pheasant-rooster.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ring-necked_pheasant_at_LaCreek_National_Wildlife_Refuge_(51154749494).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Pheasant rooster. Green head, red face, white neck ring, copper body, very long pointed tail."},"photo-g-pheasant-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-pheasant-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Charles J. Sharp, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Common_pheasant_(Phasianus_colchicus)_hen.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Pheasant hen. Mottled buff brown, long pointed tail, no colour on the head."},"photo-g-turkey-tom":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-turkey-tom.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Zion National Park, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wild_Turkey_(6384983627).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Wild turkey tom. Huge dark bird, bare red and blue head, beard hanging from the chest, fans its tail."},"photo-g-ruffed-grey":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-ruffed-grey.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: 72426950scott, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruffed_Grouse_(1).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Ruffed grouse. Small crest, barred brown or grey body, fan tail with one wide dark band near the tip."},"photo-g-wolf-black":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wolf-black.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Yellowstone National Park, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wolf_at_Biscuit_Basin_(50087877481).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Grey wolf. 30 to 50 kg in BC, long legs, broad blocky muzzle, short rounded ears. Black, grey or white."},"photo-g-coyote-snow":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-coyote-snow.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Yathin S Krishnappa, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canis_latrans_(Yosemite,_2009).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Coyote. 9 to 23 kg, slim, narrow pointed muzzle, tall ears, bushy tail held low."},"photo-wigeon-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/wigeon-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Judy Gallagher, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:American_Wigeon_(male)_-_Anas_americana,_Reifel_Sanctuary,_Ladner,_British_Columbia.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"American wigeon drake. White forehead and crown (the baldpate), green band behind the eye, pink brown sides, small blue grey bill."},"photo-wigeon-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/wigeon-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Mdf, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anas-americana-004.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"American wigeon hen. Plain grey head, rusty orange sides, short blue grey bill with a black tip."},"photo-green-winged-teal-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/green-winged-teal-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Rhododendrites, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green-winged_teal_drake_(83852).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Green winged teal drake. Tiny duck, chestnut head with a green swoosh, white vertical bar in front of the wing."},"photo-green-winged-teal-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/green-winged-teal-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Mike's Birds from Riverside, CA, US, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Female_Green-winged_Teal-_Bolsa_Chica_Wetlands_(4412427221).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Green winged teal hen. Very small brown duck, small dark bill, green wing patch."},"photo-gadwall-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/gadwall-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Department of the Interior. U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service. National Conservation Training Center. 10/1997-8888, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gadwall_Drake_-_DPLA_-_3a0518ab1519a6044a5182c72add2cba.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Gadwall drake. Grey all over, black stern (rear end), dark bill, white patch in the wing."},"photo-gadwall-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/gadwall-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hen_Gadwall_at_J_Clark_Salyer_NWR_(29622615338).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Gadwall hen. Mottled brown, orange sided bill with a dark top, white square in the wing (a mallard hen shows blue)."},"photo-shoveler-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/shoveler-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drake_Northern_Shoveler_at_J_Clark_Salyer_NWR_(42589430525).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Northern shoveler drake. Big spoon shaped bill, green head, white chest, rusty sides."},"photo-shoveler-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/shoveler-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Charles J. Sharp, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_shoveler_(Spatula_clypeata)_female_Marken.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Northern shoveler hen. Brown like a mallard hen, but with a long, wide spoon bill."},"photo-wood-duck-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/wood-duck-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Rhododendrites, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wood_duck_drake_vocalizing_in_Central_Park_(86815).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Wood duck drake. Swept back green crest, white chin straps, red eye and bill base."},"photo-wood-duck-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/wood-duck-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Russ, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wood_duck_hen,_mill_pond_(35953689361).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Wood duck hen. Grey brown, white teardrop eye ring, small crest."},"photo-common-goldeneye-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/common-goldeneye-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: CheepShot, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Winthrop_Harbor_(13334802213).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Common goldeneye drake. Green black head, round white cheek spot, yellow eye, white sides."},"photo-barrows-goldeneye-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/barrows-goldeneye-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barrow%27s_Goldeneye_Drake_Seedskadee_NWR_(16656643482).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Barrow's goldeneye drake. White crescent (not a round spot) in front of the eye, more black on the back and sides."},"photo-bufflehead-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bufflehead-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Mike's Birds from Riverside, CA, US, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Male_Bufflehead_(4239833567).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bufflehead drake. Tiny, mostly white, with a large white wedge on the back of a dark head."},"photo-bufflehead-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bufflehead-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Mdf, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bufflehead hen. Very small, dark head, one white oval patch on the cheek."},"photo-ring-necked-duck-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/ring-necked-duck-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Chuck Homler d/b/a Focus On Wildlife, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ring-necked_duck_(Aythya_collaris)_-_Las_Cruces_-_New_Mexico_-_USA_(cropped).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Ring necked duck drake. Black back, grey sides with a white spur at the front, white ring around the bill."},"photo-lesser-scaup-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/lesser-scaup-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Chuck Homler d/b/a Focus On Wildlife, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drake_Lesser_Scaup_(Aythya_affinis)_Barengat_Inlet,_New_Jersey,_USA.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Scaup drake. Black at both ends, white sides, grey back, yellow eye, blue bill."},"photo-lesser-scaup-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/lesser-scaup-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Chuck Homler d/b/a Focus On Wildlife, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hen_Lesser_Scaup_(Aythya_affinis),_Barnegat_Inlet,_New_Jersey,_USA.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Scaup hen. Brown diving duck with a bold white patch around the bill base."},"photo-canvasback-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/canvasback-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Judy Gallagher, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canvasback_(male)_-_Aythya_valisineria,_Cambridge,_Maryland.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Canvasback drake. Red brown head, long sloping black bill and forehead, bright white back."},"photo-redhead-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/redhead-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Rhododendrites, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Redhead_in_Central_Park_(15503).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Redhead drake. Round red head, grey back, blue bill with a white ring and black tip."},"photo-canada-goose":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/canada-goose.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Joe Ravi, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canada_Goose_(Branta_Canadensis).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Canada goose. Black head and neck, white chin strap, brown grey body, long neck."},"photo-cackling-goose":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/cackling-goose.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: VJAnderson, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cackling_Goose_02.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Cackling goose. Looks like a small Canada goose: short neck, tiny stubby bill, square head."},"photo-snow-goose":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/snow-goose.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Paul Danese, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20250118_snow_goose_barnes_boat_launch_PD000302.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Snow goose. White with black wing tips; pink bill with a dark grin patch."},"photo-bd-mountain-quail":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-mountain-quail.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Alan Schmierer, CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountainquail_(cropped).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mountain quail: straight plume, white bars on red sides. No open season. Never shoot it."},"photo-bd-spruce-pair-bc":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-spruce-pair-bc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Pymaxio, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Male_and_female_spruce_grouse_Nelson_BC.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Spruce grouse (Franklin's form): male black with a red comb and white spots above the tail; hen barred."},"photo-bd-wt-ptarmigan-fall":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-wt-ptarmigan-fall.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: John Hill, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White-tailed_Ptarmigan,_Rocky_Mountains,_Alberta.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"White tailed ptarmigan: white tail in every season. Willow and rock ptarmigan have black tails."},"photo-bd-rock-ptarmigan-male-winter":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-rock-ptarmigan-male-winter.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Tim Bowman, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lagopus_muta2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Rock ptarmigan male in winter: all white with a black stripe through the eye."},"photo-bd-pheasant-cock-flight":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-pheasant-cock-flight.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Tom Koerner, USFWS Mountain-Prairie, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ring-necked_pheasant_flying_Lacreek_National_Wildlife_Refuge_(15008410261).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Pheasant cock in the air: dark head, white ring, copper body. Only cocks are legal in BC pheasant seasons. A plain brown bird with a long tail is a hen."},"photo-bd-american-coot":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-american-coot.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Frank Schulenburg, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:American_coot_at_Gray_Lodge_Wildlife_Area-0097.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"American coot: slate black, white chicken bill. Not a duck; its own daily limit."},"photo-bd-pied-billed-grebe":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-pied-billed-grebe.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Frank Schulenburg, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Non-breeding_pied-billed_grebe-6514.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Pied billed grebe: small brown diver, thick pale bill. Grebes have no open season."},"photo-bd-mallard-eclipse":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-mallard-eclipse.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mallard_Drake_in_Eclipse_Plumage_(54308903041).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Eclipse mallard drake: looks like a hen, but the bill is plain yellow, not orange and black."},"photo-bd-gray-partridge":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-gray-partridge.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Åsa Berndtsson, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rapph%C3%B6na_Grey_Partridge_(14334064297).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Gray (Hungarian) partridge: orange face, grey breast, chestnut flank bars. Smaller than a chukar."},"photo-bd-snow-geese-flight":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-snow-geese-flight.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Nolabob, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snow_Geese_inflight2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"White goose overhead with black wing tips: snow goose (or Ross's). All white wings and much bigger: a swan, never legal."},"photo-bd-whitefront-snow-flight":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-whitefront-snow-flight.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Mike Budd, U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service Midwest Region, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White-fronted_geese_and_snow_geese_in_flight_(51158269114).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mixed flock: the brown geese with barred bellies are white fronts, the white ones with black wing tips are snow geese. Separate limits."},"photo-bd-mallard-speculum":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-mallard-speculum.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mallard_Speculum_(34431869295).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mallard speculum: blue patch with white bars on both sides. Same on drakes and hens."},"photo-bd-band-tailed-pigeon":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-band-tailed-pigeon.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: aroid, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patagioenas_fasciata_-San_Luis_Obispo,_California,_USA-8_(1).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Band tailed pigeon: yellow bill and feet, white neck crescent. Not the town rock pigeon."},"photo-bd-tundra-swan":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-tundra-swan.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Dominic Sherony, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tundra_Swan_(Cygnus_columbianus)_(8571142484).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Tundra swan: all white, black bill, far bigger than a snow goose, no black wing tips. Never legal."},"photo-dusky-grouse-male":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/dusky-grouse-male.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: YellowstoneNPS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dusky_grouse_male_in_the_sagebrush_(53482944105).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Dusky grouse male. Slate grey, long dark tail with a pale grey band at the tip. Big for a grouse."},"photo-ruffed-grouse-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/ruffed-grouse-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Mdf, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bonasa-umbellus-001edit1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Ruffed grouse. Fan tail with one dark band near the tip, small crest, barred body. Aspen and alder bottoms."},"photo-sharp-tailed-grouse":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/sharp-tailed-grouse.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Cephas, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tympanuchus_phasianellus_campestris_GNP_03.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Sharp tailed grouse. Pale, spotted (not barred) below, short pointed tail with white sides in flight. Grassland and aspen edges."},"photo-spruce-grouse-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/spruce-grouse-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Alan Covington, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canachites_canadensis_323749881.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Spruce grouse hen. Heavily barred, smaller than a dusky grouse, sits tight in pine and spruce."},"photo-mallard-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/mallard-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Charles J. Sharp, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mallard_drake_(anas_platyrhynchos).JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mallard drake. Green head, white neck ring, chestnut chest. Blue purple speculum edged in white."},"photo-mallard-hen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/mallard-hen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Dave Hosford, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anas_platyrhynchos_-USA_-female-8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Mallard hen. Brown, orange and black bill, blue purple speculum with white edges on both sides."},"photo-pintail-drake":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/pintail-drake.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWSAlaska, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_pintail_drake_(51102248085).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Northern pintail drake. Brown head, white neck stripe, long needle tail. Slim and long necked."}}